    "notes": "Today is Mon 12 Oct 2026, pay is the last Friday (30 Oct), window 12 to 29 Oct. As the dated-statement scenario: card Alpha closes on the 3rd, is due on the 28th by full Direct Debit from Barclays, its balance is -600 with 150 spent after the close, so the closed statement estimate is 450 due Wed 28 Oct (inside the window). Without a plan that 450 is the card's payment and Left to spend is 900. Alpha now has a repayment plan, a fixed 150 each pay period from 12 Oct paid from Barclays. G475: the plan replaces BOTH the learned series and the statement estimate for that card, so neither the 200 nor the 450 is a bill. The only bill is council tax of 150 on 20 Oct: 1,500 - 150 = 1,350 closing and lowest point. The plan reserves its 150 for this period at Barclays: after payments and plans 1,350 - 150 = 1,200, Spend from 1,200, Left to spend 1,200. Nothing is short, no cover move, at risk 0."
